This module introduces functions in Python.

A function is a reusable block of code designed to
perform a specific task. Functions help organize
programs into smaller, manageable, and reusable units,
making code easier to read, maintain, test, and extend.

Functions are one of the fundamental building blocks of
Python programming and are widely used in real-world
applications.

Python supports two main categories of functions:

1. Built-in Functions
   Functions provided by Python such as print(), input(),
   len(), type(), range(), and many others.

2. User-defined Functions
   Functions created by programmers using the "def"
   keyword to perform custom tasks.

Learning Objectives
-------------------
1. Understand the purpose of functions.
2. Learn how to define functions.
3. Learn how to call functions.
4. Understand function parameters.
5. Understand return values.
